               <persName xml:id="n1" xml:lang="ar">النواوي٬ محي الدين ابو زكرياء يحيى بن شرف بن مري </persName>
               <persName corresp="#n1" type="transliterated">al-Nawāwī, Muḥyī al-Dīn Abū Zakariyyā' Yaḥyā b. Šaraf b. Murī</persName>
               <floruit>7th/13th century<note>He studied at the Madrasa al-Rawāḥiyya in Damascus. There he first studied medicine but then he went over to Islamic learning. He began to write in 655/1257 and  in 665/1267 he was called to the al-Ašrafiyya dār al-ḥadīt in Damascus in succession to Abū Šāma. His reputation as a scholar -and as a jurist above all- was enormous</note>
               </floruit>
